# Sage Ink — window opacity (superseded, kept for history — DO NOT reapply)
#
# FOUND live by the indigo-glass simulator's /desktop/kwin/ page, 2026-09-25:
# this file still shipped opacityactive=88 / opacityinactive=85 forced onto
# EVERY window (wmclass=.* + the *rule=2 "Force" type), i.e. a global 85-88%
# translucency rule — exactly the material CLAUDE.md says was deliberately
# removed ("opaque flat ink ... no translucency", v5, 2026-08-28) and that
# scripts/install.sh's own comment above the (removed) apply step disavows:
#
#   "No global window-opacity rule is written any more (Sage Ink v5,
#    2026-08-28). Ink windows are opaque - tokens.toml [opacity].
#    window_active/window_inactive are both 1.00 now (were 0.92/0.85). This
#    block used to write a NEW uuidgen-keyed rule on every run, which is
#    non-idempotent ... Don't recreate it."
#
# install.sh has not applied this file since v5; nothing currently installs
# it. It was left on disk with its pre-v5 values, so anyone who found it and
# ran the kwriteconfig6 commands by hand would have reintroduced the exact
# translucency bug the tokens.toml change fixed. Emptied of instructions on
# purpose — a truly opaque global rule would be a no-op over KWin's own
# default (100%), so there is nothing to append here. If a kwinrulesrc need
# ever comes back, start from a fresh `uuidgen` and opacity 100 / no opacity
# keys at all, never these numbers.
